From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:34:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Add g16_init_macos for macOS's INIT
 words outside Main

macOS 26B123 sets words in the J604's init objects outside Main that
this encoder leaves at its own value. Add a load-time bit mask, default
0, that writes them at this firmware's (25G83) offsets, one group per
bit:

  0x01  Runtime +0x250 = 0: the firmware's log printer writes nothing
  0x02  Runtime +0x3d8 = 0xff: eight per-index enables
  0x04  Runtime +0x2c8 = a zeroed table of 256 counters, which the
        firmware writes without a null check on one work path
  0x08  Power: 18 controller words at offsets equal in both builds
  0x10  Power: 5 words at inferred offsets
  0x20  POWER_PERFORMANCE: 4 words (only with g16_fw_controllers)
  0x40  POWER_PERFORMANCE: 2 words at inferred offsets (same)
  0x80  Globals P-state selectors at the top row at INIT, not S1

Each object's offset map comes from paired firmware readers of the two
builds. Power +0x128 is left out: while it is set the firmware skips
its power step, and macOS clears it after INIT.

With 0 the encoded objects are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
